<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anna Maria Luisa de' Medici</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1667">1667</a>–1743</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Electress Palatine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anna Maria Luisa de' Medici, Electress Palatine, was the last member of the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-medici">Medici family</a> of Tuscany. Daughter of Grand Duke Cosimo III and widow of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elector-palatine">Elector Palatine</a> Johann Wilhelm, she returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> in 1717. By the Family Pact of 1737 she left the Medici collections of art, books and treasures to the Tuscan state on condition that they never leave Florence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anna-maria-luisa-de-medici.jpg" alt="Anna Maria Luisa de' Medici" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jan Frans van Douven · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Electres_Anna_Maria_Luisa_de%27_Medici.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
